To implement the Sobel edge detection algorithm with Gaussian filtering in MATLAB, you can follow these steps:

1. Import the input image.
2. Convert the image to grayscale.
3. Apply a Gaussian filter to reduce noise.
4. Apply the Sobel operator in x and y directions separately.
5. Combine the edge images from both directions.
6. Display the edge image.

Here's the modified MATLAB code for implementing the Sobel edge detection algorithm with Gaussian filtering:

```matlab
function edge_image = sobel_with_gaussian_filter(input_image)
    % Read input image
    input_image = imread('image.jpg');

    % Convert to grayscale
    gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);

    % Apply Gaussian filter
    kernel_size = 5; % Size of Gaussian kernel (odd number)
    sigma = 1.5; % Standard deviation of Gaussian distribution
    gaussian_kernel = fspecial('gaussian', kernel_size, sigma);
    filtered_image = filter2(gray_image, gaussian_kernel, 'replicate');

    % Apply Sobel operator in x direction
    sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
    edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');

    % Apply Sobel operator in y direction
    sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
    edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

    % Combine edges in both directions
    edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

    % Display edge image
    imshow(edge_image);
end
```

