Here's the R code to check if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric:

```R
# Function to check if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric
can_convert_to_numeric <- function(x) {
  # Check if any element is NA
  if (any(is.na(x))) {
    return(FALSE)
  }

  tryCatch({
    as.numeric(x)
  }, error = function(e) {
    return(FALSE)
  })
}

# Example usage
x <- c("1", "2", "3", "4", "5")
y <- c("6", "7", "8", "9", NA)
z <- c("A", "B", "C", "D", "E")

print(can_convert_to_numeric(x)) # Output: TRUE
print(can_convert_to_numeric(y)) # Output: FALSE
print(can_convert_to_numeric(z)) # Output: FALSE
```

