Here's a simple React utility to remove widows. This function will check if a string has a single word on a line and remove it if it does. You can use this function in your React components as needed.

```javascript
import React from 'react';

const removeWidow = (text) => {
  const lines = text.split('\n');
  const updatedLines = lines.map((line) => {
    const words = line.trim().split(' ');
    if (words.length === 1) {
      return '';
    }
    return line;
  });
  return updatedLines.join('\n');
};

export default removeWidow;
```

